  "rules": [
    "Model exhibits a strong upward drift bias (approx +20 EUR over 30 days) when recent history shows high volatility or prior spikes, failing to account for mean reversion.",
    "When sentiment is neutral (0.00) but recent price action includes significant drops (>5%), the model fails to incorporate immediate downside pressure and continues its upward trajectory.",
    "The model systematically overshoots true outcomes by 15-25 EUR in the first 10 days of the forecast horizon, ignoring the volatility clustering seen in the last 3 days of history.",
    "In periods where sentiment is mixed (positive/negative) but recent price action is trending down, the model ignores the negative momentum and predicts a steady rise instead of a volatile range or decline.",
    "The model fails to react to 'spike' events in the immediate past (e.g., 76.67 in Example 1), treating them as temporary noise rather than potential mean-reversion triggers."
  ]
}
